# Hot Fudge Sauce

Alex’s Family recipe

{ rating="5" image="hot_fudge_sauce.jpeg" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] 2 oz [unsweetened chocolate]{ ing="unsweetened-chocolate" }
- [ ] 2 Tbsp [butter]{ ing="butter" }
- [ ] 1/3 cup [boiling water]{ ing="boiling-water" }
- [ ] 1 cup [sugar]{ ing="sugar" }
- [ ] 2 Tbsp [corn syrup]{ ing="corn-syrup" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [vanilla]{ ing="vanilla" }

## Recipe

1. Melt [butter]{ ing="butter" } and [chocolate]{ ing="unsweetened-chocolate" } over low heat. Stir and blend well, then add the [boiling water]{ ing="boiling-water" }
1. Stir and blend well, then add the [sugar]{ ing="sugar" } and [corn syrup]{ ing="corn-syrup" }
1. Let the sauce come to a boil, stirring slowly over low heat. Simmer for about 5 minutes, stirring occasionally
1. Add [vanilla]{ ing="vanilla" }

## Notes

1. If using Cocoa powder, for every 1 oz chocolate, use 3 Tbsp cocoa powder + 1 Tbsp butter
